[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pulls/2171","id":4844599471,"node_id":"PR_kwDOT-9fds8AAAABIMK4rw","html_url":"https://github.com/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pull/2171","diff_url":"https://github.com/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pull/2171.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pull/2171.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/issues/2171","number":2171,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"fix(R9-OVERLAP-GREEN): main_green's overlap read is one pass, not a completion wait","user":{"login":"hpo-author[bot]","id":331381602,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOE8B7Yg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70032254?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/hpo-author","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpo-author%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Head\n\n`fix/overlap-main-green-once` at ddfd4e9abe13f29a649150da8144681e41fd4a3e, a merge of origin/main 664a4c05e into the branch plus the `counted_wait_ci` `beat` passthrough (previous head d0bf50475731788bfdae9b0bcee9cf9b90cf025d). Against current main the PR is one file, `tools/audit/seat/merge_train.py`, +71/-12.\n\n## The defect, measured live\n\nUnder `--overlap`, `main_green()` still called the **blocking** `wait_ci(tip, only=req)` before its log-only branch: the loop waits for every required context at main's tip to reach COMPLETED, so each batch paid a silent **40-60 min** pre-admission window after every main merge. Measured today with a faulthandler stack: `batch:934 → main_green:895 → wait_ci:400 (sleeping)`, sitting through #2170's push-run window. The docstring says \"does not wait\"; the code waited for completion.\n\n## The fix\n\nUnder `self.overlap`, `main_green` now does a **single** non-blocking check-runs read and logs the not-green names, exactly as the log-only branch always claimed. The non-overlap path is unchanged (same blocking `wait_ci`, same Stop). The fetch+parse is extracted as `_check_runs`/`_by_name`, shared with `wait_ci` rather than duplicated — `duplication_copies` is at its budget (37 <= 37, unchanged).\n\n## Self-test arms\n\n- **overlap + fresh main push run**: a required context still `in_progress` at main's tip — the batch starts immediately (rc 0, both entries merge), the not-green read logged once at \"before admission\", no completion wait.\n- **non-overlap unchanged**: the same pending main is still waited to completion and stops the batch (`main:` + TIMEOUT, two polls read, nothing merged).\n- **the wire arm**: counts `wait_ci` **invocations** at main's tip — zero under `--overlap`, exactly one without the flag.\n\nFull `merge_train.py --self-test`: 125 checks, 0 failed. `tests/structure.py`: ratchet passed, no budget raised.\n\n## Gate\n\n`tools/audit/seat` is not code-owned; the `hpo-author` App approval suffices per the orchestrator's standing verdict plan.\n\n## Mutation proof\n\nn/a: no behavioral branch to kill — the change replaces a polling loop with one read on one flag; the two arms pin both sides, and the stub's `cr_reads` counter plus the pending/in_progress clock is the perturbation the first arm fails under the old blocking call (TIMEOUT, rc 1).\n\n## Null control\n\nn/a: the second arm is the null control — with the flag off, the identical world still waits to completion and stops, pinning that only the overlap path changed.\n\n## Figures\n\n- `python3 tools/audit/seat/merge_train.py --self-test` → `merge_train self-test: 125 checks, 0 failed` (at ddfd4e9a). Arithmetic: the branch carried 114 checks (its base's 113 + the counting arm added in this PR); main 664a4c05e carried 122, of which 11 are arms this branch's base lacked — #2169's heartbeat arms and the #2170 additions main carried past the branch's base. The merged count is the union, 125, with no check from either side lost.\n- `python3 tests/structure.py` → `STRUCTURE RATCHET PASSED`; duplication: `RESULT duplication_copies=37 count`, `ok duplication_copies 37 <= 37` (main re-recorded the corpus at 37).\n\n## Red checks\n\n`fast (3.14)`: red in this branch's history — caused by two main-data defects this merge carried in, not by this diff, and both already fixed on main by #2173: (1) the closures lane-balance pole, whose fix is #2173's optimality arm plus the closure re-record; (2) the ci-budget `coord_footprint` row, whose fix is #2173's cherry-picked re-record from #2175. The cheaper detector for each is the check that fired (the closures lane-balance check; the ci-budget row check) — each went red on a stale main-side data table before #2173's re-record, and a branch-only run of the tool self-test and structure ratchet never touches them.\n\n## Forward-carry\n\nnone: no later stage's behavior changes — `--overlap`'s log-only contract now matches its docstring; callers are unchanged.\n\n## Friction\n\nunclear: cost: the first cut of the new arm's assertion required the log prefix `OVERLAP: main at`, which only matches a base literally named `main` — the rehearsal base logs `OVERLAP: batch/base`. A predicate written from one arm's fixture silently over-fired into the next; widened to the `OVERLAP: ` prefix.\n\n## Update at ddfd4e9a: main folded in (664a4c05e) + the wire arm's beat passthrough\n\nThe naive `git merge origin/main` conflicted in `tools/audit/seat/merge_train.py`, both hunks in the region this PR and #2169/#2170 both touched. Resolution preserved both semantics: main's heartbeat `wait_ci` (the `beat` parameter and time-based beat block) kept, but routed through this PR's `_check_runs`/`_by_name` helpers instead of its inline fetch (one paginated read in one place, shared with `main_green`'s overlap read); main's `branch_holder`/`holder_refusal`/`carry_refusal` kept verbatim; this PR's `main_green` one-pass overlap read kept as main never edited it. One integration fix the conflict hid: the wire arm's `counted_wait_ci` wrapper grew the `beat` passthrough (it wraps `wait_ci`, whose signature main extended, and the proofs call it with `beat=` — without the passthrough every proof arm dies on `TypeError`, which the first self-test run showed). The counting arm still counts `wait_ci` invocations only; the heartbeat changed no call shape it observes. All figures above re-derived at this head.\n","created_at":"2026-10-13T14:16:16Z","updated_at":"2026-10-13T21:44:28Z","closed_at":"2026-10-13T21:44:25Z","merged_at":"2026-10-13T21:44:25Z","merge_commit_sha":"400317cca4c50e239436e0c2a9fd4f89f915cea6","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pulls/2171/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pulls/2171/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/issues/2171/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/statuses/ddfd4e9abe13f29a649150da8144681e41fd4a3e","head":{"label":"tvofi:fix/overlap-main-green-once","ref":"fix/overlap-main-green-once","sha":"ddfd4e9abe13f29a649150da8144681e41fd4a3